## Contract
{{ frame_doc }}
{{ contract }}
`{{ zone_file }}` must `export function build{{ zone_name }}(ctx) → THREE.Group` where
`ctx = { THREE, env, heightAt, MATS, rand }` (`rand()` is a seeded PRNG in [0,1)). Name the returned
group `"{{ zone_name }}"`. Add instances of the listed assets at sensible real-world spacings
(paths 1.2-2 m wide, trees ≥ 3 m apart, benches facing the view), rotate them for variety, and add
zone-local detail from primitives (kerbs, gravel patches, planters, ropes, steps). Everything rests
on `heightAt(x, z)` (lowest point touching the ground, never sunk > 2 cm, never floating).
Optional `group.userData.tick = (t, dt) => {...}` to animate local things (lantern flicker, sway).

## DO
- Use the asset sizes above to avoid overlaps: keep ≥ 0.3 m between footprints unless stacking is intended.
- Prefer `InstancedMesh` or reuse of one built asset group (`.clone()`) for ≥ 5 copies.
- Keep the zone ≤ 250 lines and ≤ 400k triangles.

## DON'T
- No lights except small point lights for lanterns (≤ 4 per zone); no cameras; no sky/ground here.
- No DOM, no textures, no fetch, no Math.random (use `ctx.rand`).
- Do not import assets marked NOT AVAILABLE; do not edit other files.
